# Negative control — puts the design system's `Link` back as the tile tag. Its
# cva base carries `rounded-xs`, and `cn()` calls bare `twMerge` with no custom
# token config, so `rounded-card` and `rounded-xs` BOTH survive the merge and
# the emitted CSS order decides. The linked tile renders at 2px against the
# panels' 12px — the FE walkthrough defect 2.
#
# Intended RED:
#   Metric — a stat tile wears one radius, linked or not >
#     gives a tile that links somewhere the card radius and no competing one
#     wears the same radius whether it links or not
#
# The UNLINKED tile stays green: it was never the `Link`, which is why the two
# forms disagreed with each other and why the pair is asserted together.

